# React Server Components (next-dato)

## Async Server Components

- `async function` pages/layouts/blocks may `await` data and `getNonce()`.
- **Sync** Server Component must not render **async** child (e.g. `SeoManager`, `JsonLdScript`) — React error: *"Element type is invalid. Received a promise..."*.
- Fix: make parent `async`, or use sync [`JsonLdScriptSync`](../../src/components/patterns/seo-manager.tsx) with nonce resolved upstream.

## Client boundaries

- `"use client"` only for: accordion, nav menu, theme toggle, forms with hooks, draft chrome.
- Pass serializable props from Server → Client; no server-only secrets.

## Error boundaries

| File | Renders |
|------|---------|
| `app/error.tsx` | `<div>` UI only — **no** `<html>` / `<body>` |
| `app/global-error.tsx` | Full document replacement (rare) |

Nested `<html>` inside `<main>` causes hydration loops and repeated reloads.

## Structured Text blocks

- `StructuredTextBlockView` is sync; async block components (`export async function FaqGroupBlock`) are valid as direct return from `case`.
- Do not wrap Server blocks in `dynamic()` unless they are client components.

## SmartLink + Button

- `Button asChild` + `SmartLink` → always `tone="inherit"` on SmartLink.

## Anti-patterns

- Async component imported into client component without proper boundary
- JSON-LD async script inside sync ST block without async wrapper
- Multiple sticky `top-0` chrome layers
